 right so it's  like i'm japanese  you know um joe is portuguese and i have  you know  chinese friends and i have my hawaiian  friends and so the same thing goes with  food  is when you say hawaiian food the  average person's idea of what hawaiian  food is  it's not wrong but we can dive into it a  little bit more  dive into some of the best hawaiian food  you'll ever see  and taste is exactly what we did so this  is laulau  and lao lao is taro leaves right here  that we're gonna take some fish and some  pork that we've seasoned just with salt  i'm gonna teach you how to wrap it up  i'm gonna teach you how to finish it off  this okay  all right go ahead and season this baby  nice season that we're good yeah  okay confidence love it okay so we have  a pork belly  i want you to take one of the big leaves  like this and the simplicity  of this is the fact that right if you  think about it there's tao leaf  yeah fish pork salt four ingredients  that's it that's it what more do you  need in life keep it simple right  kiss so take a couple pieces go ahead i  like to take one with plenty meat more  fat  a piece of fish like that i'm gonna take  it  one two wrap it up  next take my tea leaf nice little  nice little pouch i'll say the pod yeah  a little packet  and there is more than one way to wrap  la la  this is just this is the way i wrap it  i'm gonna tie  a single knot that's a single overhand  okay  square knot it's like a special package  delivery great  and here's the package maybe the most  important thing to understand about mark  naguchi  is this he does not chase what's  trending at the  expense of what's necessary something  the hawaiians call  pono you say pono  over popularity always what does that  mean for you  you gotta do what's right you know it's  your kuleana your responsibility to do  what's right  here in hawaii for so many of us that  are born and raised we are tied here  genealogically you know like the way  that a lot of us look at it is like  when we mess up we don't have that we  don't have the option of like oh  you know i shaved my i shamed the name  or i got myself into trouble with the  law i'm gonna move  so i think that there's that strong  sense of  doing what's right or you know living my  life with  abandon it's not an option  when we asked for a spot to set up his  dish presentation  naguchi selected the exact opposite of a  white tablecloth  this is a real tailgate it is it is this  is so local style  the presentation included dishes  prepared by naguchi  as well as some of his favorite  selections from two hawaiian  institutions  highly a family favorite for takeout and  helena's  owned by craig ketsuyoshi who's  continuing a tradition  started by his grandmother both have  been around for more than  70 years and craig kosyoshi is known for  pipicola so pipi beef cola  string and it's essentially beef jerky  that the paniolos you know they came up  with and  it was their way to preserve beef but if  you want to try it yeah  so that one right there oh yeah nice big  yeah  you got to get the fat on there you got  to get the fat you got to get that oil  also on the menu squid luau  pastel stew poi kalua pig  tarot root and salt meat watercress  stew you'll find watercress coming out  of you know the corners of most loi like  wetland  you know wetland tower fields it grows  so  you know it was this very humble almost  peasant  sort of vegetable to me this has a lot  of heritage because if you think about  it  you know when as plantation people  our local food what came about because  we had a lack of resources  and it was cultivated by the most  resourceful of people  then there's the adobo chicken pieces  marinated in soy sauce and spices  pan fried and stewed until tender now  adobo is filipino  so now you see right we have this  amalgamation we got this sort of little  party going on  of all kinds it's a good party yeah it's  a good party  it's a great party for dessert a  hawaiian  coconut pudding what do you say  refreshments what do you want your  legacy to be  oh that's easy when i die  i want my wife to say that i was a good  husband i want my children to say that i  was a great dad  and i want my community to say that mark  noguchi didn't waste space  that's all i want he's not wasting space  uh-uh  it's a ten hour flight six thousand  miles so we could not have food here  unfortunately  um and i am unabashedly a mark naguchi  fan he was  it's so easy to be a fan of his i love  that he gave  others some shots that's exactly right  that was just  such a moment for me and his piece and  he is a part of that community  he is not wasting space no way

